From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wenwen Fu <wenwfu@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] weston: start from the primary DRM device event

The default Weston unit is enabled by graphical.target and therefore waits
for the regular boot target chain. Start it from the primary DRM device
event instead, so Weston is launched as soon as the display device is ready.

DefaultDependencies is disabled for QuickBoot activation. Keep explicit
shutdown ordering because the normal service dependencies are no longer
added automatically.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [QuickBoot activation is distro policy]

Signed-off-by: Wenwen Fu <wenwfu@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 weston.service | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/weston.service b/weston.service
index b7e845e..66006dd 100644
--- a/weston.service
+++ b/weston.service
@@ -7,0 +8 @@ Description=Weston, a Wayland compositor, as a system service
+DefaultDependencies=no
@@ -13 +14,2 @@ Requires=systemd-user-sessions.service
-After=systemd-user-sessions.service
+#After=systemd-user-sessions.service
+After=dev-dri-card0.device
@@ -16 +18 @@ After=systemd-user-sessions.service
-After=plymouth-quit-wait.service
+#After=plymouth-quit-wait.service
@@ -20 +22 @@ Wants=dbus.socket
-After=dbus.socket
+#After=dbus.socket
@@ -27,0 +30,2 @@ Before=graphical.target
+Conflicts=shutdown.target
+Before=shutdown.target
@@ -33,5 +39,6 @@ ConditionPathExists=/dev/tty0
 [Service]
+Restart=on-failure
 # Requires systemd-notify.so Weston plugin.
 Type=notify
 EnvironmentFile=@sysconfdir@/default/weston
 ExecStart=@bindir@/weston --modules=systemd-notify.so
